# highway -- portable SIMD/vector intrinsics, and the thing libjxl decodes with.
#
# Packaged only because libjxl requires it: libjxl's third_party/highway
# submodule directory is EMPTY in the release tarball (GitHub archives omit
# submodules), so its CMakeLists falls through to find_package(HWY 1.0.7) and
# stops with a FATAL_ERROR if no system highway is installed. See pkgs/libjxl.
#
# Not an LFS package, so it is pinned here rather than in versions.env. BLFS
# 12.4 is the book this desktop tier follows, and it carries 1.3.0.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/google/highway/archive/1.3.0/highway-1.3.0.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=07b3c1ba2c1096878a85a31a5b9b3757427af963b1141ca904db2f9f4afe0bc2
SRC_DIR=highway-1.3.0

# A GitHub archive URL ends in the bare tag, so without this the tarball would
# be cached as "1.3.0.tar.gz".
SRC_FILE=highway-1.3.0.tar.gz

# -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF IS LOAD-BEARING AND MUST NOT BE DROPPED. Without it this
# package DOWNLOADS SOURCE FROM THE NETWORK DURING CONFIGURE. The chain is four
# defaults deep and no single one of them looks alarming:
#
#   CMakeLists.txt:808  include(CTest)              -- CTest defaults BUILD_TESTING to ON
#   CMakeLists.txt:810  if(BUILD_TESTING AND HWY_ENABLE_TESTS)   -- HWY_ENABLE_TESTS defaults ON
#   CMakeLists.txt:816  if(NOT HWY_TEST_STANDALONE) -- defaults OFF except on MSVC, so this is true
#   CMakeLists.txt:817  if(HWY_SYSTEM_GTEST)        -- defaults OFF, so the else branch runs:
#   CMakeLists.txt:820  # Download and unpack googletest at configure time
#
# That last branch shells out to cmake twice to fetch and build googletest, and
# raises FATAL_ERROR if either step fails. Two ways it is wrong here, and the
# first is the one that matters even where the network is reachable: every other
# source in this tree arrives through fetch.sh with a sha256 verified before
# unpacking, and this would pull an unpinned tree in behind that. Second, the
# builder image has no CA bundle, so the fetch fails and takes configure with
# it -- which is at least loud.
#
# BLFS passes the same flag, for the narrower stated reason that gtest is not in
# the book. Recorded here in full because "tests are off" reads like payload
# avoidance, and this is not that.
#
# -DHWY_ENABLE_EXAMPLES=OFF: defaults ON and builds programs that are then not
# installed. Nothing needs them and they are pure build time.
#
# NOT SET, deliberately:
#
#   BUILD_SHARED_LIBS   _scripts/build-cmake.sh already passes it as ON, and it
#                       has to be: highway's own CMakeLists.txt:561 declares
#                       option(BUILD_SHARED_LIBS ... OFF), so the default is a
#                       STATIC-ONLY build. libjxl links libhwy, so a static
#                       highway would give it nothing to link and the failure
#                       would surface in the next package rather than this one.
#                       Passing it again here would be a second source of truth
#                       for a value the shared script already gets right.
#   HWY_ENABLE_CONTRIB  left ON, its default. libhwy_contrib.so is part of what
#                       BLFS installs and it costs little; libjxl links only
#                       libhwy, but the .pc and cmake package files describe the
#                       full set and trimming it would make this install differ
#                       from the book for no gain.
#   HWY_ENABLE_TESTS    left ON, its default, and this one is a JUDGEMENT rather
#                       than an oversight, so it is recorded. It does NOT gate
#                       the googletest download -- BUILD_TESTING above already
#                       does, and either alone is enough (CMakeLists.txt:810 is
#                       an AND). What it gates is the INSTALL of libhwy_test.so
#                       and libhwy-test.pc (CMakeLists.txt 718-732 and 753-764);
#                       add_library(hwy_test) at 643 runs either way, so turning
#                       it off saves no build time, only files.
#
#                       KNOWN WART, inherited from the book: because
#                       HWY_TEST_STANDALONE is OFF on non-MSVC, libhwy-test.pc
#                       is written with `Requires: gtest` (CMakeLists.txt
#                       755-760) and NOTHING IN THIS TREE PROVIDES gtest. So an
#                       installed .pc names a package that does not exist. It is
#                       left as the book has it because nothing here queries
#                       libhwy-test -- libjxl wants libhwy and the cmake config,
#                       not this -- and because BLFS ships libhwy_test.so as
#                       part of the set. If it ever does bite, the fix is
#                       -DHWY_ENABLE_TESTS=OFF, which drops both the library and
#                       the .pc; noted here so the next reader does not have to
#                       re-derive it from four defaults.
CMAKE_ARGS="-DBUILD_TESTING=OFF -DHWY_ENABLE_EXAMPLES=OFF"
